Package: PhysioAppKit
Title: Domain-Neutral Single-Case Engine for Physiological Application Layers
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person("Yusuke", "Matsui", email = "mail.to.matsui@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A small, domain-neutral engine for single-case (N-of-1) analysis
    shared by physiological application layers (rehabilitation, sport,
    psychophysiology, and others). Provides the Nonoverlap of All Pairs (NAP)
    effect size, a threshold-and-band single-case analysis, a phase plot, an
    honest hypothesis-to-evidence verdict combiner, and a dependency-free Rasch
    model for turning ordinal ratings into an interval scale. Application layers
    supply their domain slots (ontology, threshold, goal, reasoning, report) and
    call this engine; the engine knows nothing about any specific domain.
